Hi Team,

Thanks everyone for a fantastic Q2. Here's a summary of what we
accomplished and what's ahead for Q3.

-- Q2 HIGHLIGHTS --

1. Performance Improvements
   We reduced P95 API latency by 40% through query optimization
   and connection pooling. The new indexing strategy cut full-text
   search times from ~800ms to ~50ms on average.

2. Infrastructure Migration
   The move from bare-metal to Kubernetes is now 80% complete.
   All stateless services have been migrated. The database stateful
   set migration is scheduled for the first week of July.

3. Developer Experience
   We shipped the new local development environment based on
   Docker Compose. Setup time for new engineers went from 2 days
   to under 2 hours. The feedback has been overwhelmingly positive.

4. Observability
   We now have distributed tracing across all critical paths
   using OpenTelemetry. Alert response times have improved
   significantly thanks to better correlation between services.

-- Q3 OKRs --

Objective 1: 99.99% Platform Reliability
  KR1: Reduce P99 latency to under 200ms for all user-facing APIs
  KR2: Achieve 99.99% uptime for the core sync engine
  KR3: Implement automatic failover for the database tier

Objective 2: Product Velocity
  KR1: Ship the new composer with real-time collaboration
  KR2: Reduce release cycle from 3 weeks to 1 week
  KR3: Achieve 90% test coverage on critical paths

Objective 3: Team Growth
  KR1: Hire 3 backend engineers and 2 SREs
  KR2: Complete the engineering onboarding documentation
  KR3: Start the internal tech talk series

-- DISCUSSION ITEMS FOR THE RETRO --

Please come prepared to discuss:

  * What slowed us down most this quarter?
  * What should we START doing that we aren't doing now?
  * What single change would have the biggest impact on Q3?

We'll be meeting in the usual conference room (B-42) at 2 PM.
Lunch will be provided.

Looking forward to a productive session!

Cheers,
Charlie
Engineering Lead

